Z||000000||p4n1c||12-22-2000||11:32 AM||||Does anybody know where I can find auto shift knobs(I don't know what else to call them) that look like the Fiero or '88 Cutlass sport shifter?  Or know if you can re-cover existing ones?<P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||12-22-2000||11:39 AM||||I have a stock Fiero one from my 86 SE sitting on a shelf. I am using a Bonneville SSE "cobra head" shifter handle. You can use any GM shift handle from the 80's to mid 90's. The non-leather ones are about $10-$20 at a dealer and the leather ones are anywhere from $50 to $120 depending on style.||||reg||1
Z||000002||p4n1c||12-22-2000||11:42 AM||||Cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I like the Cutlass sport shifter, so maybe I'll see if I can grab one from the wreckers and re-cover it.  I'm mostly like Steve(darklord) right now, just thinking up mods to do to the car, it's not worth it to buy a car now, so I'm waiting for the spring.<P>I think a black(or dark grey)/red combo would look nice for an interior(if done properly, hints of red, instead of blasting someone with colour  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  Momo has the "Race" style steering wheel in black/red.<P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||6
